      "id": "theverge-2026-09-02-belkin-s-kid-friendly-wireless-headphones-are-25-percent-off",
      "title": "Belkin’s kid-friendly wireless headphones are 25 percent off",
      "summary": "The SoundForm Mini 2 come in a variety of colors, and include a carrying case if you’re willing to spend a bit more. | Image: The Verge\t\n\nVerge readers can get a discount on Belkin’s SoundForm Mini 2 wireless headphones. The kid-focused on-ear headphones feature an 85-decibel volume limit and easy controls, and a mode that lets them beam audio (wired or wirelessly) to a second pair without extra h",
      "body": "Verge readers can get a discount on Belkin’s SoundForm Mini 2 wireless headphones. The kid-focused on-ear headphones feature an 85-decibel volume limit and easy controls, and a mode that lets them beam audio (wired or wirelessly) to a second pair without extra hardware. Readers can use the code VERGE25OFF to save 25 percent on up to two pairs of SoundForm Mini 2 headphones.\nThe $29.99 model without the zip-up carrying case gets knocked down to $22.49. Alternatively, a more limited selection of colors are currently available that include a case, which is $29.99 instead of $39.99 once the offer code is applied in the cart.\n[Product: Belkin SoundForm Mini 2 headphones | https://belkin.evyy.net/c/482924/214281/3736?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.belkin.com%2Fp%2Fwireless-on-ear-headphones-for-kids%2FAUD012fqPU.html, https://belkin.evyy.net/c/482924/214281/3736?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.belkin.com%2Fp%2Fwireless-on-ear-headphones-for-kids%2FAUD011fqPUCS.html]\nWhile these don’t deliver noise cancellation, they should be good enough for most situations. They can last up to 55 hours on a single change, and they can fold up neatly to fit into a variety of bags. The SoundForm Mini 2 are made for ages 3 and up, and feature an adjustable headband and cushioned earcups. They’re pretty no-frills, though the audio-sharing mode I described above is a great way around having to buy some sort of audio splitter or wireless transmitter to ensure multiple kids are entertained.\n* Onto more capable headphones, the Sonos Ace have been succeeded by the $449 Ace Ultra that offer better battery life, improved noise cancellation, plus the feature we most wished was in the original: the ability to directly link them to speakers via Wi-Fi, letting you move freely around your home instead of close to your soundbar. Those are sizable improvements, but the original Sonos Ace is still a fantastic value, especially at the current $299.99 sale price from Amazon and Best Buy. While not a new discount, it’s nice to have a lower-cost alternative available. In our 2024 review, we bemoaned the iffy state of the Sonos app, and criticized the Ace for not working with the Beam and Ray soundbars for TV Audio Swap. The company recently debuted its plans for overhauling the app, and TV Audio Swap support for those soundbars has been added following their debut.\n* Kirby Air Riders for the Nintendo Switch 2 is close to $20 off for the physical version at Amazon, which is its lowest price yet. You can snag it for $51.99, while the digital version is still selling for $69.99. While not an essential Switch 2 title for those building out their libraries with a limited budget, it delivers F-Zero-esque frenzy that Mario Kart World can’t match. It’s the follow-up to Kirby Air Ride on the GameCube, giving players more flexibility in who they race as, what aircraft they use, plus a host of game modes to give you more to do than just racing. Read our review.\n* If you’re in the mood to shop, but you’re not quite sure what you want, it might be worth taking a spin through the Amazon Resale catalog of returned products. Many products are marked down by up to 30 percent once you add them to your cart. Just look for the green “Save at checkout” on product listings where Amazon Resale is the seller. The percentage of savings differs per product. I didn’t find any earthshaking deals on consoles or other big-ticket items, but you can save a good amount on things like controllers and headphones.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Deals",
        "Gadgets",
        "Verge Shopping"
      ],
