      "id": "bbc-2026-09-02-lucy-letby-boyfriend-doctor-named-as-court-order-lifted",
      "title": "Lucy Letby 'boyfriend' doctor named as court order lifted",
      "summary": "Dr Mark Deakin, a consultant at Alder Hey hospital, was described as Letby's \"boyfriend\" during her trial.",
      "body": "Letby - who has always maintained her innocence - is serving 15 whole life prison terms. The Criminal Cases Review Commission (CCRC) is conducting a review of Letby's convictions.At her criminal trial - the longest murder trial in UK history - Deakin gave evidence in relation to several babies. He was granted special measures as well as anonymity. These allowed him to give evidence from behind a screen so that Letby, the public gallery, and the media were prevented from seeing him.Deakin's evidence provided detail of some of the emergency calls and resuscitations which he and Letby were jointly involved in. Their long nights of text messaging were laid bare and many of the messages shown to the jury.When he was sworn in, on the first occasion he testified, Letby burst into tears, in what was the first display of emotion from her during the trial.During her cross-examination, Letby was forced to deny that Deakin was her boyfriend, though she did accept that they had gone on a trip to London together.The prosecuting barrister, Nick Johnson KC, said Letby \"tried to get out the back of the dock\" when the doctor first came to the witness box.Letby said: \"Yes, because I felt unwell.\"Johnson said: \"No, it's because you didn't like hearing your boyfriend giving evidence, did you?\"Letby said: \"That's unfair.\"Prosecutors also went through a WhatsApp message exchange between Letby and a friend who had teased her for being \"flirty\" with Deakin.Johnson said: \"She knew you were sweet on Mark, didn't she?\"Letby said: \"What do you mean, sweet?\"Johnson said: \"That you had a crush on him.\"\"No,\" said Letby.\"There was nothing between me and that Mark.\"Johnson told the court that Letby told her friend she had received a \"strange message\" from the doctor.Her colleague responded: \"Did you? Saying what? Go Commando [laughing face emoji].\"While some media reports have described him as \"a key witness\", Deakin was one of many former colleagues of Letby's whose joint testimony helped to build the prosecution case against her, and none of the convictions rested solely on his evidence.Correction: The original version of this story was published with an incorrect picture which has since been amended",
