      "id": "hackernews-2026-09-02-telli-yc-f24-is-hiring-engineers-and-designers-berlin-on-sit",
      "title": "Telli (YC F24) is hiring engineers and designers [Berlin, on-site]",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://careers.telli.com/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49533557\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "There’s a certain type of service you never forget.\nYou call, and they remember who you are.\nYou talk, and they know what happened last time.\nYou need support, and they help you on the spot.\nYou are busy, and they know when to leave you alone.\nThe type of conversation that makes you feel understood.\nThe type of service that shows that you’re cared for.\nThe type of interaction that's actually worth having.\nBut over the past decade, this kind of service has become increasingly rare. Instead we got:\nChatbots that forget what you said five minutes ago.\nForms that ask what you’ve already answered a 100 times.\nTickets that reduce you to just another number in the system.\nCall queues that make you want to throw your phone out the window.\nBusinesses had to make these tradeoffs in order to scale their service. But this is changing.\nAt telli, we are building AI to run customer-facing operations.\nWith agents that don’t just answer questions. But act, understand, learn, and improve.\nThe future won't be a world where businesses simply automate their customer interactions with AI.\nBut a world where every interaction has context, attention, and intent.\nA world where every interaction is worth having.Finn zur MühlenPhilipp BaumannsSeb Hapte-Selassie",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "sebselassie",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-02T08:43:49.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://pub-bb2e103a32db4e198524a2e9ed8f35b4.r2.dev/91526b0d4c10138ce7f07a9b073d5940/id-preview-aca7f041--832d1ce1-6784-40c9-ae2d-e12352025283.lovable.app-1788338940773.png",
