      "id": "hackernews-2026-09-01-show-hn-weedout-safari-extension-that-hides-youtube-ai-label",
      "title": "Show HN: Weedout – Safari extension that hides YouTube AI-labeled videos",
      "summary": "I'm the developer. I built this because AI-generated conspiracy videos were getting out of control in my own YouTube feed. Weedout is a $1.99 Safari extension for macOS that removes videos YouTube labels “Made with AI” from feed, search, related videos, playlists and Shorts. It uses YouTube's label rather than AI detection, runs locally, and does not catch unlabeled videos.\nSource for developers w",
      "body": "FOR YOUTUBE · SAFARI · MACOS\nVideos YouTube labels “Made with AI” — quietly pulled\nfrom your feed, search, related videos and Shorts before you scroll past them.\nNo blocking screens, no drama. The weeds are just gone.\nSimulated. On a real feed a weed is gone in about half a second — cached ones never sprout at all.\nFilters AI-labeled videos out of home, search, related, playlists and Shorts shelves\nAuto-skips AI-labeled Shorts in the Shorts player (optional)\nDim mode wilts weeds in place instead of removing them, so you can verify before you trust it\nNo accounts, no tracking, no data collection — everything runs on your Mac\nDetection relies on YouTube’s own “Made with AI” disclosure badge — no guessing,\nno heuristics, no false accusations. Unlabeled slop is out of scope (for now).\nQuestions, bug reports, or a weed that slipped through?\nEmail masteranza@gmail.com — include the video link if it’s about detection.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "masteranza",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-01T22:06:57.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://masteranza.github.io/weedout/screenshot.png",
      "originalUrl": "https://masteranza.github.io/weedout/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
