      "id": "bbc-2026-09-01-we-ll-find-way-to-save-jodrell-bank-burnham-says",
      "title": "'We'll find way to save Jodrell Bank,' Burnham says",
      "summary": "Burnham said \"there is no way that we can see its demise, and it won't happen under my Government\".",
      "body": "Prime Minister Andy Burnham has vowed to save the UK's largest telescope at the Jodrell Bank Observatory.The Lovell telescope, which has stood in Cheshire since 1957, is the world's third-largest steerable radio telescope.But in July this year, UK Research and Innovation (UKRI) said the site would not be prioritised for further funding after its current agreement ended in March 2028.Burnham said: \"Every one of my generation went on a school trip to Jodrell Bank, and there is no way that we can see its demise, and it won't happen under my government.\"UKRI said its decision for the site was \"the result of a comprehensive, evidence-based prioritisation process\".The Prime Minister spoke of his determination to save the site after being asked a question about its future in the House of Commons. Congleton MP Sarah Russell, whose constituency includes the Jodrell Bank site, said it \"is facing a significant problem in the medium term because of funding cuts\".She called on Burnham and No 10 North to work alongside her and Macclesfield MP Tim Roca to address the issue.Burnham said: \"I know there are changes that have been made in relation to research funding, but Jodrell Bank is a heritage asset for the country, as well as a research asset.\"He said he would set up the meeting she requested, adding: \"There must be a way to save Jodrell Bank, and I give a commitment today, at this despatch box, we will find it.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-01T19:30:02.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/62ff/live/6961bcf0-892e-11f1-b684-d3f861a1f4cf.png",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm2qj7jzl7no?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
