mats, and surfaces it early enough for our customers to act. We are a small team of engineers plus security, privacy and fraud specialists. Pre-seed, $2.25M led by Moonshots Capital: https://www.infohawk.com/news/2026-06-08-pre-seed-funding-an...You’d own how data gets in: scrapers and collectors that survive source changes, official APIs where they exist, undocumented endpoints where they don’t. Sources break constantly. Can you figure out how to use AI to spot the change and adapt automatically? Stack: TypeScript, Node, SvelteKit, Postgres, Playwright, heavy AI-assisted development.We’re looking for ~3-5 years building scraping or integration systems in production, but if you’re a great engineer who doesn’t tick every box we’d still like to hear from you. UK-based for London, US-based for NYC; we cannot sponsor visas. Two of our three founders are engineers, one in each city, and you’ll work with them directly.james@infohawk.com\nOhr | Data Engineer + Software Engineer | REMOTE (US) | $140K–$200K + EquityOhr is reinventing industrial chemistry from the atom up—turning breakthrough science into industrial alchemy.We're hiring two engineers to help build the computational infrastructure behind it:Data Engineer — Build the data foundation connecting laboratory instruments, scientific data, enterprise platforms, analytics, and AI systems.Software Engineer — Build production AI tools, molecule-discovery applications, internal systems, and digital twins for processes scaling from lab to manufacturing.We're looking for builders excited to learn the science and have their code touch the physical world. 4–8 years experience. U.S. person status required due to export-controlled systems.Data Engineer: https://ohr.xyz/careers/5f2b1267-f692-4be6-b796-bd7e8cf53ee3\nORIGAMICS | Founding Researcher | San Francisco | ONSITE/REMOTEOrigamics is building AI models that reason about electronics and help turn schematics into production-ready boards.We’re looking for a Founding Researcher to work directly with the founders on physics-informed models for Electronics design — physical behavior, simulation, and scientific ML. You’ll tackle open-ended research problems, push models from experiments to production and real hardware, and have the opportunity to publish novel research along the way.You’ll likely be a good fit if you have strong ML/research fundamentals, enjoy 0→1 problems, and have experience with scientific ML, geometric deep learning, numerical methods, simulation, EE, or applied physics. PhD is a plus, not a requirement.Apply: https://www.origamics.ai/join-us?ashby_jid=7acf3a2d-46a5-420...\nBoom Supersonic | https://boomsupersonic.com/ | Senior, Staff, Principal Software Engineer | ONSITE Denver, CO | Full-time | $180k - $225k + EquityHelp us build an AI-first engineering, manufacturing, and supply chain platform. What if you could ask AI: \"how does this new turbine blade geometry affect our 42MW power requirements?\" And actually get a meaningful answer? This is the platform that supports Superpower, Symphony, and Overture from design to deployment across multiple factories. If you love hard-tech, distributed systems, web apps, and building AI infrastructure at scale, please apply.Also hiring for telemetry and engine design and analysis software roles.Apply here: https://ats.rippling.com/boom-supersonic/jobs/21b8325e-66aa-...Feel free to email me at mark[dot]miller[at]boom.aero\nPascal | Founding Engineer | New York City\nPascal’s mission is to equip the offline economy with foundational intelligence, starting with the consumer packaged goods (CPG) sector. We’re reworking the archaic data foundation for agents that automate outcomes: recover lost revenue, optimize sales, and proactively resolve operational breakdowns.We are ex-MIT founders who have built at startups that have grown from six to nine figures in revenue. We have raised $5M from institutional investors and angels of category-defining businesses (Decagon, Cognition, etc.)