gibility.Email sasan at inferra.ai with anything relevant. For internships: please tell what you'd like to do in the next ~year, if you could do anything.\nSteg.AI | Machine Learning Engineer | Irvine, CA (Onsite) | Full TimeSteg.AI develops AI-powered watermarking technology to protect and authenticate digital media. Our invisible watermarks are imperceptible to humans but robustly detectable by our proprietary models. Founded in 2019, we're an NSF- and investor-backed startup in Orange County, CA, with a team of 6 PhDs in computer vision.We're hiring a Machine Learning Engineer to help push the frontier of AI for watermarking, steganography, and media provenance. You'll take state-of-the-art steganography models and own their journey to production — optimizing and deploying them on desktop and cloud platforms, serving as the link between research and customer-facing products.Responsibilities: productionize novel steganography models, build inference pipelines, integrate models into cloud platforms, benchmark performance, and turn research into maintainable production code.Required: PyTorch, ONNX export, experience deploying deep learning models to the cloud, Python and C/C++, strong cross-team communication.Bonus: background in steganography/watermarking/media provenance, video/image codecs, MLOps tooling, CV/ML publications or open-source contributions.To apply, send your resume to careers@steg.ai\nEnrollment123 | https://e123insurtech.com | Staff Platform Engineer | REMOTE (US) | Full-timeWe are SaaS platform that connects Insurance Carriers, Agencies and Agents, and enables sales to consumers.My team is hiring a Staff Platform Engineer to keep things running smoothly and help our engineers modernize and build new products.We are responsible for:    - security for PCI and HIPAA data\n- AWS infrastructure that serves millions of people every month\n- developer tools and infrastructure to allow our teams to deliver\n- data engineering and operational support\n- automation, monitoring, and on-call rotations (especially during Open Enrollment!)\nOur stacks include:    (70% --) SQL Server + ColdFusion\n(25% ++) Postgres + node/typescript\nIt's not a flashy product or stack I'll admit, but we have a lot of opportunities to improve the product and a lot of growth potential to expand our impact. Happy to tell you more!If you're interested, email me at jjay+orangesite@enrollment123.com with your honest, hand-written resume. I don't want some super polished AI bullshit, show me your real experience! The interview process is hopefully short and sweet: 1) meet with me for a quick intro to ensure we'll be a good mutual fit, 2) advance to a technical interview with the team, then 3) a last culture + company info session so you have all the info to make a decision.Sorry, given our industry and size, you must be in the US and able to work without visa sponsorship.\nShared Context Lab | Member of Technical Staff | San Francisco or New York | ONSITE | Full-timeShared Context Lab (https://sharedcontextlab.com) is building adaptive personal AI that understands the texture of real life: relationships, routines, responsibilities, and goals. Our closed beta is garnering very positive feedback and retention. We’re venture backed + incubated at iconic design firm IDEO.We’re looking for a senior, hands-on engineer to tackle:- Core agent, product, and infrastructure systems- Context, memory, orchestration, and tool use- Simulation environments for users, schedules, relationships, and multi-agent interactions- Evaluations for long-horizon agent behavior, reliability, and safetyWe care a lot about high agency, collaboration, and high ownership mentality. Strong product judgment and care for user experience matter as much as technical rigor.Apply here: https://sharedcontextlab.com/mts or reach out at join@sharedcontextlab.com\nODK | Senior Product Manager | Remote (Worldwide) | Long-term contract, 30–40 hours/week | $90–$110/hour USDODK is an open-source platform used by thousands of organizations worldwide to collect billions of data points for disease surveillance, supply chain traceability, environmental monitoring, and more. It enables users to build powerful forms and reliably collect structured data, even in places with little or no Internet connectivity.ODK has been actively developed for 18 years. We have a mix of self-hosted and SaaS users across many sectors. We're looking for a senior product manager who will own product discovery and prioritization across this diverse user base. To be successful, you'll need to find the common needs behind very different workflows and turn them into opinionated product improvements.Because the team is small and the user base is large, this is a high-autonomy role where product decisions have an unusually direct impact. You should have substantial experience managing complex B2B or technical products. Experience with open source, self-hosted software, and small, fully remote teams is a plus.Details and application: https://getodk.org/about/jobs/senior-product-manager\nMechanize | San Francisco, CA (Onsite) | Junior SWE ($300k + equity + bonus), SWE ($350k + equity + bonus), Research Engineer, Alignment ($300k-$400k + equity + bonus)Applying takes <2 min: https://www.mechanize.work/apply/We build environments that frontier AI labs use to train their models to do real-world software engineering. We have more demand than we can keep up with, so we're hiring fast.\nIt’s so interesting that the example training given is game boy advance emulator as such a large task, when misalignments and task veering happen so regularly in smaller bits.\nTelescope Partners | Software Engineer & Data Scientist | On-site US, San Francisco | Full-timeTelescope is an early stage growth VC firm with a focus on enterprise software companies. We're a small, efficient team, with a beautiful office in Presidio. We work closely with entrepreneurs and help them fill critical business functions as they grow. Our tech team is mostly oriented at team efficiency and improving investment decision-making using data. This involves replacing as much investor work and intelligence with automation as possible. If you're interested in PE, agents, and data science, then this might be a good role for you!We’re looking for someone  with 3-10 years of experience.To apply email mike at telescopepartners.com\nAnterior | Software Engineers | NYC | Onsite | Full TimeAnterior is improving the experience of healthcare for everyone. Our agentic orchestration platform makes clinical decisioning frictionless for RNs and MDs.About You: You have a passion for doing things The Right Way, you believe Less is More, you want to focus on Foundations of system design and architecture (pacelc, consistency guarantees), you care as much about what code you do not write, you’re tired of the hype treadmill and care about the fundamentals. You have battle scars from overengineered and underperforming slop, and you care about writing code that lasts.- Langs: TS / Python - Infra: Nix, CDKTF, AWSWe’re hiring from infra to full stack. Come share your proudest firefighting story with us in an interview, bring your GitHub, and let’s see if we’re a good fit!Dev log: https://xn--xp5a.anterior.appsaul@anterior.com\nPostHog | Full-Time | Technical CSMs, Technical Content Writers, AI Research Engineer | REMOTE (all remote) | Hiring GMT-8 to GMT+2 | PostHog makes your product self-driving.\n* we have a public handbook (posthog.com/handbook) if you want to learn how we work, pay and more in complete detail.* we are growing through more autonomy and transparency not through process.* we have a ton of scale and a bunch of super interesting technical problems to solve* we're building 20 more products over the next couple of years, so you could end up building one of those* public compensation calculator! see immediately what you'd get paid* we're hiring: ai research engineer, technical customer success managers (americas & emea), technical account executives, technical content writers, bdr team lead, SREs (americas), clickhouse engineer, and more.https://posthog.com/careers\nGreywatch | Co-Founder & CEO | REMOTEGreywatch is building an AI security and governance platform that gives companies visibility into how AI agents are operating across their infrastructure, from the kernel to the network.We’re actively looking for a *Co-Founder & CEO* to take an existing MVP and early commercial pipeline to market and help scale the company.We’re looking for someone with experience in early-stage / 0-to-1 company building, enterprise B2B sales, developer-focused or open-source products, and ideally fundraising. Experience selling to CIOs/CISOs and a strong understanding of AI security are particularly relevant.The role includes significant equity, substantial autonomy, an existing MVP, and early commercial traction.Apply here: https://greywatch.co/careers/co-founder-ceoQuestions: [apply@greywatch.co](mailto:apply@greywatch.co)\nAstronomer | https://astronomer.io | NYC preferably, open to remote | Full-timeHiring for ~10 eng roles listed at astronomer.io/careers, but the focus is specifically on distributed systems, observability, and applied AI.Astronomer is a primary contributor to Apache Airflow and offers our customers a managed Airflow service with a similar business model as Databricks with Spark or Confluent with Kafka. Our tech stack is primarily Go, Python, and TypeScript. The problems we work on generally center around (1) building out our commercial managed Airflow offering, (2) building a data + infra observability stack on top of Airflow, and (3) building AI products and experiences that are genuinely load-bearing and additive to our customers experience on the platform.We're also starting to write more about the work we're doing, this is pretty representative: https://www.astronomer.io/blog/astro-airflow-re-engineered-f...Apply using our website or email me - my email is 