nction; we expect you to be making forward progress, not simply responding to tickets.Because this role has some physical hardware responsibilities, we'd prefer it be filled by someone in the above localities, even though the vast majority of the role can be performed remotely.You will join a high-caliber team where collaboration, honesty, and open communication are at the core of everything we do.Search term bingo: Help Desk, Information Technology, LAN, Networking, MDM, Mobile Device Management, Systems Administration, Network Administration, Security, Cloudflare, Systems Engineer\nHello Sam,Is there a link to the IT Associate opening because couldn't find it on your company site especially for the DC area or is it better to email you directly? Thanks.\nFurtim Modus | Hiring Java Developer (Full-Time) | NYC (HYBRID) | $125K-$250K + equity | https://www.furtimmodus.com/software-engineerWe are currently seeking a talented and driven Java Developer to join our team full-time. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute your skills and expertise to a venture backed funded fintech trading firm with emphasis in US equities capital markets tech based out of the New York City and in exchange we’ll provide you with base comp $125k-$250k, full benefits, cash bonus, and equity.Requirements:- Electronic trading server-side software development experience- Experience in Open Source technologies such as Aeron Transport, Aeron Cluster, Aeron Archive, Artio, and Agrona is a big plus- Experience with Adaptive Hydra trading platform is a plus- Experience with US equities trading venues is a plusBenefits:- Flexible hybrid schedule to accommodate other commitments- Collaborative and supportive team environment- Relocation assistance to NYC Metro areaIf you are passionate about Java development and interested in joining a fintech venture, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your resume if interested to agency@furtimmodus.com in this opportunity.-----Furtim Modus | Hiring Data Engineer (Full-Time) | NYC (HYBRID) | $100K-$150K + equity | https://www.furtimmodus.com/data-engineerWe are currently seeking a talented and driven Data Engineer to join our team full-time. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute your skills and expertise to a venture backed funded fintech trading firm with emphasis in US equities capital markets tech based out of the New York City and in exchange we’ll provide you with base comp $100k-$150k, full benefits, cash bonus, and equity.Requirements:- You will work with Snowflake, AWS, PostgreSQL, Sigma Computing, Grafana, Prometheus, and VictoriaMetrics to develop reliable data pipelines, organize business-critical datasets, deliver analytics, and improve platform observability.Benefits:- Flexible hybrid schedule to accommodate other commitments- Collaborative and supportive team environment- Relocation assistance to NYC Metro areaIf you are passionate about data engineering and interested in joining a fintech venture, we would love to hear from you. Please submit your resume if interested to agency@furtimmodus.com in this opportunity.\nVersaFeed.com | SENIOR SOFTWARE ENGINEER (Python/Django + JavaScript - VueJS/React) | REMOTE (USA ONLY) | Full-timeAbout us: Fancy ETL pipeline which processes products from huge ecommerce companies. Data extraction and massage, delivery to destinations like Google/Meta/TikTok/etc. Profitable, 18+ yrs stable, 100% employee-owned. No VC, no pointless meetings, just serious coding.Stack: Python/Django, JavaScript, VueJS/React, Docker, Git, PostgreSQL/Snowflake/DuckDB, Dagster, AWS + Strong agentic coding skills (Claude Code / Codex)Compensation: $150K–$220K USD/year DOE.You: 5+ yr senior dev who's seen (and fixed) enough dumpster-fire code to last a lifetime. Python/Django deeply internalized; solid JS skills and able to wrangle Vue/React. You rock backend data pipelines like old jeans: Dagster, Snowflake, DuckDB, Postgres - in the cloud or on your bitchin' VM rack. Docker and Git