      "title": "The full scale of the UK's forced adoption scandal revealed",
      "summary": "Exposing a British scandal.  The women forced by the state to give up their newborns",
      "body": "Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food         Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live             Home            News            Sport            Weather            iPlayer            Sounds            Bitesize     CBeebies     CBBC     Food        Home     News     Sport     Business     Technology     Health     Culture     Arts     Travel     Earth     Audio     Video     Live         Close menu\nA-ZTV GuideWatchlistHomeStolen BabiesStolen BabiesContains some upsetting scenes.Contains discriminatory language\nInformation and support for some of the issues covered in our programmes can be found at bbc.co.uk/actionlineRevealing how the British state forced 250,000 unmarried women to give up their babies. Told by the mothers affected, this landmark documentary exposes the forced adoption scandal. Duration1h 28mFirst shown1 Sep 2026Available for 11 monthsMore Like ThisMore Like This EpisodesColeen meets James online. He’s a firefighter, they plan to marry and he’s had a vasectomyA groundbreaking insight into the very centre of a complex and emotional trialMurder cases, minute by minute, from the critical first days through to conviction.Who Do You Think You Are?Barbara Windsor traces her maternal grandfather to the east London docks.A young mum of two is killed, defenceless victim of a savage, frenzied and brutal attackDavid Olusoga sets out once more to uncover the history of a single house in Leeds.Scotland's real-life heroes. Emotional highs and lows on frontline with ambulance crewsFrom the makers of Murder 24/7. In trauma, every second is critical.The Young Midwives Of EssexLearning the ropes, one baby at a time. The midwives balancing life on and off the wardAn investigation into Instagram and the effects it has on people's mental health.I Thought 