      "summary": "Kemi Badenoch is expected to carry out a wider reshuffle of her front bench team following high-profile departures.",
      "body": "Dame Priti was appointed to Badenoch's shadow cabinet after finishing sixth in the leadership election, and previously held senior roles in successive Tory governments, including a three-year spell as home secretary under Boris Johnson.Announcing her departure in a statement on X, she wrote: \"It has been an honour to lead the Party's foreign affairs team in Parliament over the last two years.\"I'm pleased to continue supporting Kemi and the Conservative Party in a new role strengthening our relationships with fellow conservatives and centre right parties around the world.\"She said she would continue to serve as the MP for Witham in Essex.A Conservative reshuffle had already been expected in the coming weeks because of the shadow energy secretary Claire Coutinho's upcoming maternity leave.In recent weeks, people within the party have played down speculation that the shadow chancellor Sir Mel Stride could also lose his job in the changes.But some sources within the party still believe Badenoch could choose to replace him.Many within the Conservative Party view Coutinho as a likely future shadow chancellor. The shadow energy secretary is said to have impressed colleagues with her performances in Parliament and the media.But it is unlikely Badenoch will move to appoint her as shadow chancellor while she is on leave from the front bench.The Conservative leader will also need to replace Sir James as her shadow housing secretary after he quit the front bench to focus on setting up a campaign to run for London mayor.He has not yet been selected as the party's candidate for the May 2028 election, nor has he resigned as the MP for Braintree.",
