    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-08-30-sons-of-officer-who-died-in-a66-crash-lead-out-man-utd-as-ma",
      "title": "Sons of officer who died in A66 crash lead out Man Utd as mascots",
      "summary": "The sons of PC Matthew Blades led Manchester United out at Old Trafford for Sunday's Premier League game with Ipswich.",
      "body": "The two sons of a police officer killed in a crash on Teesside led out the Manchester United team as mascots for Sunday's Premier League match against Ipswich at Old Trafford.PC Matthew Blades, described as a \"proud Red\" by United, was a regular at Old Trafford. The club paid tribute to him in Sunday's match programme, while his widow attended the game with their children.PC Blades and his colleague PC Tom Clough died in a head-on collision between their police car and a vehicle going the wrong way on the A66 near Middlesbrough early on 22 August. Five people in the other vehicle also died.United said they learned of the deaths of the two officers \"with great sadness\".\"Matthew was a proud Red, a devoted family man and a police officer who dedicated his life to helping others,\" said the club, in a tribute in the programme.At Elland Road, match officials for Leeds United's Premier League fixture against Brentford on Sunday wore black armbands as referee Tony Harrington was a friend of PC Blades.On Saturday, there was a minute's applause in memory of PC Blades and PC Clough before Middlesbrough's Championship encounter with West Brom at Riverside Stadium. Pictures of the two men were displayed on a screen.People also gathered to pay tribute at Seaton Carew FC's game against FC Hartlepool. PC Blades had been a junior football coach at both teams.Earlier this week, 17 people were arrested in connection with the investigation into the crash, bringing the total number of arrests to 24.The occupants of the other vehicle, a Passat - Michael Robert Cahill, 23, Jacob Matusiak, 23, Makai Saddington, 18, Theo Rae, 17, and Cole Robert Worthy, 17, also died.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-30T16:30:05.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/969c/live/419ac790-a48e-11f1-8395-fb1eae51ae18.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/ckg8x0ex8gno?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-08-30-british-woman-killed-in-stabbing-at-german-railway-station",
      "title": "British woman killed in stabbing at German railway station",
      "summary": "A 27-year-old German man was arrested immediately after the incident in Rosenheim, Bavaria.",
      "body": "A British woman has died after being stabbed at a railway station in southern Germany in the early hours of Sunday morning, police have said.The 31-year-old woman was attacked at the station in Rosenheim, Bavaria, shortly before 01:00 local time (00:00 BST). She was taken to hospital where she died as a result of \"severe\" injuries, the Bavarian Police said in a statement.Officers arrested a 27-year-old German man at the scene immediately after the incident. The background and motive for the attack is under investigation, the statement added.Police have asked anyone who may have witnessed \"an argument or physical altercation\" at the station late on Saturday or early on Sunday to contact them.The suspect, from the Fürstenfeldbruck district, will be brought before magistrates later on Sunday, according to German news agency DPA.It is unclear whether the two knew each other or what the woman was doing in Bavaria, DPA also reported.Rosenheim is one of the largest cities in Upper Bavaria and is a busy rail hub for passengers travelling to Austrian cities including Vienna, Salzburg and Innsbruck. The Rosenheimer Herbstfest - an event similar to the Oktoberfest beer festival - is currently taking place in the area.Responding to the attack, Rosenheim Mayor Abuzar Erdogan said \"there are no indications of a security threat in our city or of any link to our Herbstfest\".\"The criminal investigation department is working closely with the public prosecutor's office to investigate the circumstances and motive behind the crime as a matter of urgency,\" he wrote in a statement.A Foreign Office spokesperson told the BBC: \"We are supporting the family of a British woman who died in Germany [and] are in touch with the local authorities.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-30T16:11:46.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/229c/live/8e80aca0-a45c-11f1-b370-b9b7934350c8.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cx2zy118q7ko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
