      "id": "techcrunch-2026-08-27-atf-declares-major-incident-as-ransomware-gang-claims-hack",
      "title": "ATF declares ‘major incident’ as ransomware gang claims hack",
      "summary": "The ATF is the latest federal government agency in recent years to notify Congress of a \"major incident\" involving its cybersecurity.",
      "body": "10:54 AM PDT · August 27, 2026\nImage Credits:arah Reingewirtz / MediaNews Group / Getty Images\nThe U.S. Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives, or ATF, says a cyberattack on one of its systems has been declared a “major incident,” a formal, legally defined classification that prompts a formal notification to lawmakers in Congress.\nATF said in a statement that it’s responding to the cyberattack on a stand-alone system that’s separate from the bureau’s network. An ATF spokesperson told reporters that the targeted computer system contained information such as the “targets of ATF investigations.”\nTechCrunch has seen a claim of responsibility by the Qilin ransomware gang on its leak site, but it did not provide evidence for its claim, such as a sample of leaked data. Qilin is known for running a “ransomware-as-a-service” operation, in which it leases its hacking tools to other criminal affiliates for a cut of the profits. The gang has listed media giant Lee Enterprises and U.K. pathology lab giant Synnovis as targets.\nUnder federal law, “major incidents” include significant cyber incidents that are likely to cause demonstrable harm to U.S. national security or broader U.S. interests. Agencies are required to disclose major incidents to Congress within a week of their discovery.\nThe ATF joins several government agencies in recent years that have declared major incidents following a breach, including a 2023 ransomware attack on a system used by the U.S. Marshals Service, and a breach of an FBI system earlier this year that exposed phone numbers of targets under surveillance by federal agents.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Zack Whittaker",
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-27T17:54:23.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/atf-police-1233760688.jpg?w=1024",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/08/27/atf-declares-major-incident-as-ransomware-gang-claims-hack/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
