      "id": "hackernews-2026-08-26-zohran-and-the-short-link",
      "title": "Zohran and the Short Link",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://iamwillwang.com/notes/zohran-and-the-short-link/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49457512\nPoints: 163\n# Comments: 55",
      "body": "If you live in NYC and are anywhere on social media, you’ll likely have\nOftentimes, his videos announce a new project or initiative or event.\nIf the announcement is something that you can\nactively participate in, the videos also always end with a short, top-level link: nyc.gov/{initiative}.\nI love that. I think it:\nMakes government easy to engage with. It’s a human-readable\nURL that I can easily follow through on. It also funnels social media distribution into one place, owned and operated by NYC.\nSets up a pattern of interaction. nyc.gov is where I can\nexpect to interact with city government online.\nFollows up announcements with actual experiences.",
